sks. Congress should impose strict joint and several liability on frontier developers and cloud hosts instead of capping exposure. Make frontier labs risk their corporate equity when their software causes material harm.\n\nAccelerationist wants to preserve open development by tracking physical reagents like phosphoramidites under the Chemical Weapons Convention framework. That downstream strategy breaks against physical reality. Thousands of legacy benchtop gene synthesizers manufactured before 2024 lack cryptographic tracking chips and operate entirely off-grid. Enforcing border checks on bulk chemicals does nothing to prevent bad actors from orchestrating decentralized synthesis across automated domestic laboratories. Accelerationist exempts software creators from legal accountability, leaving emergency responders and local communities to absorb the fallout. When an unmonitored automated system triggers a biological disaster, who reimburses the public for the damage?",
